  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerated implementation of end Tuberculosis strategies in Ethiopia - Ethiopia (01-Jul-2024-30-Jun-2027)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia, Tuberculosis, Federal Ministry of Health of the Federal Democratic Republic of Ethiopia (FMOH)This program has the following goals: To contribute to the mission of the health sector by ending TB as a major public health problem in Ethiopia by 2030. The objectives of this program are: Address gaps in patient/client pathway..  Prevent TB infection and active disease..  Provide people-centered equitable and quality TB services..  Enhance bold policies and strengthen supportive systems..  Strengthen strategic information, research and innovations.</narrative>
  </description>
